  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=0$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=1+3x+\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{27}{8}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${f}^{\u2034}(0)?$\n\n${f}^{\u2034}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(0)}{3!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(0)}{3!} & =-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{\u2034}(0)}{6} & =-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(0) & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
